From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:30:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Take the built-in SideStore's app group and source from the
 Info.plist

Cartouche's IPA for the player's own SideStore (app/scripts/sidestore_ipa.py)
carries an app group of its own, group.com.SideStore.SideStore.cartouche,
which its Info.plist names (CartoucheAppGroup), and its own source
(CartoucheSourceURL): the player's SideStore keeps its apps in
group.com.SideStore.SideStore.<team>, and the two must never share it.

- LCSharedUtils.builtInSideStoreAppGroup is that group, or
  LiveContainer+SideStore's without the key. It must begin with
  LiveContainer+SideStore's, so that every test of the group by its
  beginning still finds it. The app group candidates and
  isBuiltInSideStoreAppGroup start from it, so that Cartouche installed
  from that IPA never opens the player's SideStore's group.
- LCSharedUtils.cartoucheAppInfo reads Cartouche's Info.plist, from the
  app or from one of its extensions, such as LiveProcess, where the
  built-in SideStore renews and updates the app.
- SideStoreHooks gives the built-in SideStore that group for its base app
  group, which it signs Cartouche again with, and the source the Info.plist
  names, https only, before the one the app is built with.
- LCTabView hands the pairing file the player's SideStore answers with
  (sidestore://pairing) to Cartouche's setup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MzPJouBNse6nNy5526AYaf
